## Examples (MOST RELEVANT)
- examples/memories/agent_memory_example.py - Example of creating a ChatAgent with memory, saving/loading memory, and running queries.
- examples/memories/agent_memory_vector_db_example.py - Example of ChatAgent using vector DB memory with memory saving/loading and querying.
- examples/toolkits/memory_toolkit.py - Example script demonstrating a ChatAgent using the MemoryToolkit with function calling to manage memory (save, load, clear).

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/memory_toolkit.py - Implementation of MemoryToolkit providing function tools to save, load, clear memory for a ChatAgent.
- camel/agents/chat_agent.py - Core ChatAgent class implementation with memory management methods (save_memory, load_memory, load_memory_from_path, clear_memory, update_memory).

## Config/Types
- camel/types/enums.py - Contains enums like ModelPlatformType, ModelType used in model and agent creation.

## Tests
- test/toolkits/test_memory_toolkit.py - Tests for the MemoryToolkit.
- test/memories/test_agent_memories.py - Tests related to agent memory functionality.
- test/memories/test_chat_history_memory.py - Tests for chat history memory.
- test/memories/test_vector_db_memory.py - Tests for vector DB memory.

These files and examples provide comprehensive references to create an agent with memory tools, manage memory, and run query examples. The example in examples/toolkits/memory_toolkit.py is especially relevant for using MemoryToolkit with a ChatAgent and function calling. The agent_memory_example.py and agent_memory_vector_db_example.py show memory usage patterns with ChatAgent. The implementation files in camel/toolkits/memory_toolkit.py and camel/agents/chat_agent.py show the underlying methods and classes to use. Tests ensure correctness of memory toolkits and agent memory.
